---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — r0" description="Privacy information for r0 website accounts.">
  <main class="policy wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">R0 ACCOUNT</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Draft for review before production account launch</p>
    <p>This draft describes account authentication on the r0 website using Supabase Auth. It is not a privacy notice for every third-party service linked from r0.</p>
    <h2>Information used for account access</h2>
    <p>When you register or sign in, Supabase Auth processes the email address and credential or provider information needed to authenticate your account. The website does not store your password in its own application database. Contact the project operator for details about data retention, account deletion, and the configured email and social providers.</p>
    <h2>Website session storage</h2>
    <p>The website uses the Supabase client to persist an authentication session in browser storage so sign-in, OAuth redirects, and password recovery can complete. You can sign out from the account panel. The desktop IDE currently manages a separate r0 account session.</p>
    <h2>Desktop application and project files</h2>
    <p>The website account page does not upload your local source code. Signing in to an r0 account does not grant access to GitHub repositories or connect an AI provider. Those integrations require their own explicit setup in the desktop application.</p>
    <h2>Service providers and configuration</h2>
    <p>Account data is handled by the Supabase project configured for this site and its enabled email or social providers. The project operator must identify the project region and providers, configure production email delivery, and review their applicable privacy terms.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For a privacy request, use the contact method listed on the <a href="https://adshkumar.is-a.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">project maintainer’s website</a>.</p>
    <p class="review-note">This draft must be reviewed and completed by the project operator before account registration is enabled in production, including applicable retention periods, legal basis, data-subject rights, and operator contact details.</p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 820px; padding-top: 120px; padding-bottom: 90px; }
  .eyebrow,.updated { color: var(--txt-3); font-size: 10px; }
  h1 { margin: 12px 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 6vw, 48px); letter-spacing: -.06em; }
  .policy p { margin: 14px 0; color: var(--txt-2); line-height: 1.9; font-size: 12px; }
  .policy h2 { margin: 30px 0 8px; color: var(--txt); font-size: 16px; }
  .policy a { color: var(--amber); }
  .policy .review-note { padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--amber-line); background: var(--amber-wash); color: var(--txt); }
</style>
